      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Standing seam metal roofing is the best premium material for Utah's climate, while Class 4 impact-resistant asphalt shingles offer the best overall budget value.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Standing seam metal roofing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah weather features heavy mountain snow, intense summer UV rays, and high winds. Different materials handle these extremes in unique ways."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Top Roofing Materials for Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Standing Seam Metal Roofing:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Pros: Smooth panels shed heavy snow fast to prevent ice dams, reflective coatings lower cooling costs, and it resists strong winds and hail."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lifespan: 50 to 70 years."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Best for: Mountain and high-elevation areas (like Heber City, Park City, or Midway) with heavy winter snow loads."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Class 4 Impact-Resistant Asphalt Shingles:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Pros: Affordable upfront cost, handles severe temperature swings, and resists hail and wind. Many Utah insurance companies offer 10% to 25% policy discounts for Class 4 ratings."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lifespan: 25 to 35 years."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Best for: Budget-conscious homeowners and lower-elevation valley homes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Concrete and Clay Tile:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Pros: Natural weight resists high winds, and tiles withstand high heat in southern desert regions."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lifespan: 50+ years."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Best for: Southern Utah or specific architectural styles, provided the home's framing can handle the heavy weight ."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
